      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-06T01:53:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this bit follows what we do for CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC where we also reset and init the PD chip.  reinitializing the TCPC means we get out of \"programming\" mode as soon as we can.\n\ni did an experiment on reef to emulate the power loss with the\nbattery cutoff.  if you do the ectool pdcontrol suspend/resume,\nthe system will go through a power-on reset as a result.\n\nthis behavior should be OK.  when we come back,\nthe update will be skipped since it has already been applied.",
      "parentUuid": "b032fe5e_9eb8aa57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2303,
        "startChar": 7,
